<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Wellkept's background piece.

	  ⭐ Copied into Wellkept.app/Contents/Library/LaunchAgents/ by a build phase declared in
	  project.yml. SMAppService.agent(plistName:) reads it from there. Registered for one user,
	  with no password and no administrator, and listed in System Settings ▸ General ▸ Login Items.

	  ⚠️ The Label and the file name are also written in App/Backup/Agent/BackgroundPiece.swift.
	  BackgroundPieceTests reads this file off the disk and fails the build if the two disagree —
	  a mismatch would register a job under one name and unregister nothing under another.

	  ⚠️ BundleProgram is the APP'S OWN executable, not a separate helper, and that is the whole
	  safety argument for this feature. macOS decides Full Disk Access from the code signature of
	  the process asking; a separate helper is a different program with a different identity and
	  would almost certainly get its own empty entry, so a scheduled backup would silently contain
	  no mail, no messages and no photos with no error reported. Same binary, same signature, best
	  chance of inheriting the grant — and AgentSight proves it at run time rather than assuming it.
	-->
	<key>Label</key>
	<string>studio.stonemesa.wellkept.agent</string>

	<key>BundleProgram</key>
	<string>Contents/MacOS/Wellkept</string>

	<!-- argv[0] is a name, not a path, because BundleProgram supplies the path. The flag is what
	     WellkeptEntry.main() branches on, before SwiftUI or NSApplication is touched. -->
	<key>ProgramArguments</key>
	<array>
		<string>Wellkept</string>
		<string>--background-piece</string>
	</array>

	<key>RunAtLoad</key>
	<true/>

	<!-- Restart if it crashes, and only then. A plain KeepAlive would fight the person who is
	     trying to stop it. -->
	<key>KeepAlive</key>
	<dict>
		<key>SuccessfulExit</key>
		<false/>
	</dict>

	<!-- ⭐ This is what makes the Login Items row say "Wellkept" instead of a raw reverse-DNS
	     label. Somebody who finds a background item they cannot place will switch it off, and
	     they would be right to. -->
	<key>AssociatedBundleIdentifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>studio.stonemesa.wellkept</string>
	</array>

	<!--
	  ⛔ Deliberately absent: ProcessType Background and LowPriorityIO. Time Machine takes them and
	  the measurement is that it gives away about 42% of its throughput to throttling and runs on
	  efficiency cores. A backup nobody is watching still has to finish.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
